    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Which of these fractions is closest to $1.45$?\n\n$1\\frac12,\\quad1\\frac{33}{50},\\quad1\\frac25,\\quad\\frac{147}{100}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{147}{100}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1\\frac12&=1.50\\\\1\\frac{33}{50}&=1.66\\\\1\\frac25&=1.40\\\\\\frac{147}{100}&=1.47\\end{align*}$$\n\nTheir distances from $1.45$ are $0.05$, $0.21$, $0.05$ and $0.02$, respectively. The smallest distance is $0.02$, so $\\frac{147}{100}$ is closest.",
